claimed: acme-pebble -- the interop the in-process fake cannot give (filed with okay-acme, 2026-09-07): our client against Pebble, Let's Encrypt's OWN test server, in docker. Proves what a double cannot -- that a real implementation accepts our JWS, our nonce handling, our POST-as-GET and our CSR, and that we read its directory, its Location headers and its problem+json. The shape: docker run pebble (14000 API over its own test CA, PEBBLE_VA_NOSLEEP=1), the CA pulled out with docker cp and trusted by a test-scope Http over the JDK client (production code untouched), our challenge server on the host port Pebble validates against, the domain host.docker.internal with --add-host so Linux behaves like Docker Desktop. Live-tagged, skipped where docker is absent. Adds okay-acme/src/test/.../TestAcmePebble.scala and a Results note in specs/acme.md.
